## version55 / stmap55

- hypothesis: Keep the reviewed `stmap54` severe-feedback branch, but cap cut-only one-sided pressure exceptions to at most `1.25` inverter areas of local area-save. This tests whether the one accepted `stmap54` `syn2` exception was worth its area cost.
- motivation: `stmap54` improved `syn2` delay by `0.36 ps` versus `stmap53`, but cost `6.53` extra area and fired only once on the required set. The campaign recommendation was to preserve the reviewed severe branch while adding a small area-ratio or area-save cap around cut-only exceptions.
- command name: `stmap55`
- files changed:
  - `src/base/abci/abc.c`
  - `src/base/abci/abcStmap_55.c`
  - `src/base/abci/module.make`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperCore.c`
  - `src/map/mapper/mapperInt.h`
  - `abclib.dsp`
