  - `.autoeda/runtime/versions.md`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json`
  - `.autoeda/runtime/last_prompt.txt`
- algorithm summary: `stmap55` is a numbered two-pass `stmap` command. It clones the `stmap54` first-pass SCL load/max-cap collection and dense sink-pressure feedback, selects the blended gain only under the same severe feedback conditions, and performs the final remap with mapper mode `56`. Mode `56` preserves the reviewed `stmap53` pressure-near branch through `Map_MatchStmap54ModeratePenaltyFactor()`, preserves the `stmap54` cut-only candidate test, then admits a cut-only exception only when `AreaSave <= 1.25 * inverter_area + epsilon`. Cap-blocked cut-only candidates are reported separately and fall back to the normal strict area gate. Existing `map` and `stmap0` through `stmap54` remain on their prior command paths and mode numbers.
